## 🧪 Testing: Reglas de Cobertura

### Obligatorio Testear

- ✅ Services (100% coverage)
- ✅ Stores (NgRx Signals)
- ✅ Utilities (pure functions)
- ✅ Repositories (mocks de Supabase)

### Opcional (Defer a v2.0)

- ⏳ Componentes (solo críticos: forms, auth)
- ⏳ E2E (Playwright para flujos completos)

### Ejemplo de Test con Vitest

```typescript
// blocks.repository.spec.ts
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';
import { BlocksRepository } from './blocks.repository';

describe('BlocksRepository', () => {
  it('should fetch daily blocks for user', async () => {
    const mockSupabase = {
      from: vi.fn().mockReturnValue({
        select: vi.fn().mockReturnValue({
          eq: vi.fn().mockReturnValue({
            eq: vi.fn().mockReturnValue({
              order: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({
                data: [{ id: '1', name: 'Deep Work' }],
                error: null
              })
            })
          })
        })
      })
    };
    
    const repo = new BlocksRepository(mockSupabase as any);
    const blocks = await repo.getDailyBlocks('user-123', '2025-01-30');
    
    expect(blocks).toHaveLength(1);
    expect(blocks[0].name).toBe('Deep Work');
  });
});
```

